.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-USER-GROUPS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-user-groups \- list Euclid user groups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam list-user-groups
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-pageSize\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-pageIndex\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sortColumn\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists user groups via the eam service's
.I list-user-groups
action. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
The JSON response, containing the matching groups (each with its member
user IDs) and the total group count, is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only return groups whose name starts with \fIPREFIX\fR. If omitted, all
groups match.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-pageSize " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of groups to return. \fI0\fR or less (the default,
\fI\-1\fR) means no limit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-pageIndex " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index, applied when \fB\-\-pageSize\fR is set. Defaults to
\fI\-1\fR (meaningless while paging is off).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sortColumn " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Field to sort by: \fIname\fR (default) or \fIdescription\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, or the caller is not an
authenticated administrator. If the failure was an expired or invalid
session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
List every group:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-user-groups
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check who the current administrators are:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-user-groups \e
    --prefix administrator
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-user-group (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-user-group (1)
